workedExamples.solution_text:
$D$ is directly below $A$, so its $x$-coordinate is $-3$. It is level with $C$, so its $y$-coordinate is $-2$.

$D=(-3,-2)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{solutionblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[color=black!20,very thin,xstep=6mm,ystep=6mm] (-4,-3) grid (3,3);
\draw[<->,black] (-4.5,0)--(3.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-3.5)--(0,3.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \n in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3}{\path (\n,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\n$};}
\foreach \n in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3}{\path (0,\n) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\n$};}
\path (0,0) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\draw[black] (-3,2)--(1,2)--(1,-2);
\draw[solutionblue,dashed] (-3,2)--(-3,-2)--(1,-2);
\foreach \p in {(-3,2),(1,2),(1,-2)}{\fill[black] \p circle (1.5pt);}
\fill[solutionblue] (-3,-2) circle (1.5pt);
\path (-3,2) node[above left] {$A$};
\path (1,2) node[above right] {$B$};
\path (1,-2) node[below right] {$C$};
\path (-3,-2) node[below left] {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

